The new Gatekeeper is substantially stronger than the earlier placeholder version. A request cannot declare its own trusted role anymore. Instead, principal_id is bound locally to a fixed role and scope. Requests are HMAC-signed over canonical JSON, have timestamp/skew checks and unique nonces, write actions require idempotency keys, legitimate retries with fresh nonces reuse their original result, and external acknowledgers can only operate on tickets belonging to their assigned scope.

I tested specifically that:

